 "verdict_as_specified": "FAIL -- STOP AND ESCALATE: a boundary-calibration error would invalidate every topological-edit dataset built on this solver",
 "diagnosis": {
  "finding": "The measured -3 dB widths of the two simulators cannot be compared with a single estimator, because the repo estimator's kappa was calibrated on ISM data and FDTD data does not carry it. FT-A already measured this: kappa_ism = 1.6608 vs kappa_fdtd = 1.0208.",
  "evidence": {
   "west_a070_x_axial": {
    "raw_gamma_over_pi": 8.289,
    "kappa_ism_calibrated": 14.067,
    "ism_measured": 14.62,
    "fdtd_measured": 9.5,
    "reading": "ISM tracks the CALIBRATED value; FDTD tracks the RAW value"
   },
   "ratio_check": {
    "ism_over_fdtd": 1.539,
    "kappa_ism_over_kappa_fdtd": 1.627
   },
   "cross_check": "FDTD uniform-alpha (1,0) measures 3.08 Hz here, reproducing FT-A's independently-run validated A2 (3.0812 Hz) exactly, so the FDTD side of the measurement is sound."
  },
  "self_criticism": "This gate committed the D54 error it was written to guard against: it scored against a target embedding a calibration assumption without stating the assumption or quantifying its error at the operating point. A 38.68% 'failure' was almost entirely kappa.",
  "corrected_specification": "Compare kappa-FREE quantities: (a) the underlying decay rate gamma from a one-pole fit on the source-deconvolved H_deconv, which is what the boundary actually sets, and/or (b) a ratio that cancels kappa (e.g. the x-axial bandwidth at alpha=0.70 divided by the same mode's bandwidth at alpha=0.15, measured within each solver). Only then is a 10% criterion meaningful.",
  "what_this_does_and_does_not_establish": {
   "does_not": "that the alpha->impedance calibration is correct -- still unverified",
   "does": "that the 38.68% discrepancy is not evidence of mis-calibration, so the STOP-AND-ESCALATE trigger is not met on this evidence"
  }
 },
 "history": {
  "first_attempt": "a raw receiver-averaged spectrum with no walk caps: it reported FDTD (1,0) = 8.77 Hz against the validated 3.08 Hz and ISM bandwidths of 6114 Hz inside a 0-300 Hz band, because unprojected neighbouring modes let the -3 dB walk run off the array. Replaced with the repo estimator on the modally-projected spectrum, applied identically to both streams."
 }
}